<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdirahman Mohamed Abdullahi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1955">1955</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Abdirahman Irro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdirahman Mohamed Abdullahi, known as Irro, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> politician and diplomat who became president of Somaliland in December 2024. A former speaker of the House of Representatives and leader of the Waddani party, he defeated the incumbent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muse-bihi-abdi">Muse Bihi Abdi</a> in the election of November 2024, and the peaceful handover strengthened Somaliland's democratic reputation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdirahman-mohamed-abdullahi.jpg" alt="Abdirahman Mohamed Abdullahi" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Madaxtooyada JSL · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_Abdullahi_(Irro).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
